-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Public domain code and published algorithms this library builds on
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TweetNaCl
  Daniel J. Bernstein, Bernard van Gastel, Wesley Janssen, Tanja Lange,
  Peter Schwabe, Sjaak Smetsers - public domain. (Basis of the X25519 code.)

poly1305-donna
  Andrew Moon - public domain / MIT. (Basis of the 26-bit Poly1305 code.)

Algorithms from publications (no code taken):
  - GCM reduction in the bit-reflected representation: S. Gueron, M. Kounavis,
    "Intel Carry-Less Multiplication Instruction and its Usage for Computing
    the GCM Mode" (Intel white paper).
  - Long division: D. Knuth, TAOCP vol. 2, algorithm D; H. Warren, "Hacker's Delight".

Constants and parameters come from the standards (FIPS 180-4, FIPS 186-4 / SEC 2,
FIPS 197) and are generated by the scripts in test/.
